      "description": "Watch Besiktas vs Kauno Žalgiris highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. The stage was set on August 20, 2026, for a compelling UEFA Europa League encounter as Besiktas faced off against Kauno Žalgiris . With the atmosphere building in the stands, both teams looked to establish dominance in a match that promised high stakes and intense tactical battles. A Blistering Opening Half Besiktas wasted no time asserting their authority, racing out of the blocks with intent. Just six minutes into the contest, Ridvan Yilmaz turned provider, setting up Hyeon-Gyu Oh for a clinical finish to open the scoring. The home side continued to pile on the pressure, and it wasn't long before they doubled their advantage. In the 12th minute, Ridvan Yilmaz was again at the heart of the action, delivering a perfect ball for Amir Murillo to find the target. The visitors from Lithuania struggled to cope with the pace and movement of the Turkish giants, who remained in complete control throughout the first half. Second Half Adjustments and Penalty Drama As the second half commenced, Kauno Žalgiris attempted to claw their way back into the game with a triple substitution, bringing on Motiejus Burba , Ilhan Fakili , and Lirim Kastrati . However, Besiktas remained composed and continued to dictate the flow of play. Their persistence paid off in the 60th minute when they were awarded a penalty. Orkun Kokcu stepped up to the spot and calmly converted, effectively putting the game out of reach. Following the goal, the home side introduced fresh legs, including Dusan Vlahovic , to maintain their offensive threat. Disciplinary Flurry and Full-Time Whistle The closing stages of the match saw a significant increase in physical play, leading to a flurry of yellow cards for both sides. Players such as Franco Baldassarra , Renan , and Anton Tolordava were cautioned as the intensity boiled over. Despite the stop-start nature of the final minutes, Besiktas managed the game professionally, with Kassoum Ouattara coming on to shore up the defense. When the referee finally blew the whistle at 90+5 minutes, it marked the end of a commanding performance by the hosts, who secured a vital result on the European stage."
