      "description": "Watch Omonia Nicosia vs St. Truiden highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 27, 2026. The UEFA Europa League stage was set for a compelling encounter on August 27, 2026, as Omonia Nicosia hosted St. Truiden . Both sides entered the pitch with high ambitions, resulting in a fast-paced match defined by clinical finishing and tactical shifts. A First Half of Penalties and Precision Omonia Nicosia wasted no time establishing their dominance in front of their home supporters. The deadlock was broken in the 16th minute when Lois Diony stepped up to the penalty spot and confidently converted to give his side the lead. The French striker was just getting started, as he doubled the advantage in the 29th minute, finishing off a well-placed assist from Ewandro . The 2-0 lead reflected Omonia's early control, but the visitors refused to collapse. St. Truiden fought their way back into the contest just minutes later. In the 33rd minute, they were awarded a penalty of their own, which Ilias Sebaoui calmly dispatched to reduce the deficit. The first half concluded as a feisty affair, with officials handing out yellow cards to Shogo Taniguchi , Senou Coulibaly , and Visar Musliu as both teams battled for every inch of grass. Diony Secures the Hat-trick and the Win The second half began with Omonia Nicosia looking to kill off the game, and they did so through the same devastating duo. In the 50th minute, Ewandro provided his second assist of the night for Lois Diony , who completed a brilliant hat-trick to make it 3-1. This cushion allowed the hosts to manage the tempo, even as St. Truiden introduced fresh legs like Oumar Diouf and Wolke Janssens to find a way back. Any hopes of a comeback were effectively ended in the 83rd minute when Nikolas Panayiotou added a fourth goal for the Cypriot side, assisted by Panagiotis Andreou . While St. Truiden managed to find the net one last time in stoppage time (90+2') through Ilias Sebaoui , assisted by Kaito Matsuzawa , it was merely a consolation. The final whistle confirmed a productive night for Omonia Nicosia , led by the clinical excellence of Diony ."
